{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>When you forbid your vineyard.</b> The Sages said: this is difficult — why was it stated? And if you ask that it was stated because of <b>after you</b> — no, for it is established that even before him he is warned regarding עוללות." "<b>You shall not glean.</b> Rashi explained: which is a עוללות? Any cluster that has neither כתף nor נטף, etc. כתף: small clusters set one upon another — meaning, small clusters emerging from its sides; and this is a solitary one that has no clusters joined to it, and they are found only sparsely. נטף: those that hang from the central stem and descend — meaning, the berries are packed close and drip downward, whereas those of this one are scattered and not packed one against the other."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:11.825358142Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}